{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Blood pressure is 128 over 78, pulse seventy six, saturation 98 percent. He is ready for you.",
  "[SEG0002] person_1 (NURSE): My little boy got sunburnt at the beach last month. Cried the whole night, so these skin things make me nervous.",
  "[SEG0003] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sit. What is the problem.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (PATIENT): Uh, there is a mole on my back, doctor. I don't know, my partner made me come.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I stay with him. That mole was light brown only, now the colour is dark in patches.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Since when.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): Err, since Diwali or after. Well actually I cannot say. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0008] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I also cannot fix the date. Festival time or a little later only.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): Did it bleed.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (CAREGIVER): Once, yes. Small spot on his vest, then it stopped by itself.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): Mm. Maybe the shirt rubbed. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Itching now. Yes or no.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Not itching.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Pain.",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): No pain.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any other skin trouble. Rashes, new spots anywhere else.",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No, nothing else. Only this one I think. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sunburns before. Yes or no.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): Many, when I was a boy. Cricket in the sun, no shirt. Bad burns, three four times.",
  "[SEG0020] person_4 (CAREGIVER): My own sister had a black mole removed in Pune last year. She is fine, that is why I got worried and brought him.",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any tablet or cream on this.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): I was taking a cetrizine tablet, ten mg, at night, for some old itch. I stopped it in March. They wrote amoxcillin five hundred also, but I never took it, not even once.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (DOCTOR): Turn around. Shirt up.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Asymmetric brown black mole on the left upper back. Border is irregular, colour is patchy, about eight millimetres. No bleeding just now and no ulcer.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): Ultraviolet light injures the pigment cells, the melanocytes. When they multiply unevenly the colour turns patchy and the border goes irregular. That is what has happened in the skin.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): So is it cancer? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): Working impression is an atypical mole. Melanoma is not ruled out. I am referring you to dermatology.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Skin OPD is booked this week. Collect the slip from reception.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): This week itself? Umm, should I put some cream?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): No cream. Do not scratch it. Use sunscreen and stay out of the midday sun. If it bleeds again, come sooner, do not wait.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (CAREGIVER): I will keep the sunscreen in his bag. He forgets.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (PATIENT): Eight millimetres, is that big? I don't know what to think.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): With these features it needs the skin specialist. No tablet from my side today.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (NURSE): I will tell reception to put the dermatology slip in his file before you leave.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Ok doctor. Thank you. I still don't know, honestly."
 ],
